From: Darrel Griet <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omapfb: minnow-panel: Restore 60Hz refresh rate

Motorola downclocked the minnow panel from 60Hz to 45Hz in 2014
(IKXCLOCK-2734 on the OMAP DISPC pixel clock, IKXCLOCK-2788/2970 on the
SSD2848 bridge), most likely to save power / avoid a flicker issue on
the shipping watch. The bridge PLL (216.6MHz) and the bridge->panel
MIPITX link (108.3MHz) are unchanged between the 60Hz and 45Hz configs -
60Hz was the factory-native rate over this same link - so the only
differences are the OMAP pixel clock and the SSD2848 VTCM pixel-clock
ratio register [0x0010]. Restore both:

  - panel-minnow.c: DISPC pixel_clock 320*290*45 -> *60 (4176 -> 5568 kHz)
  - panel-minnow-common.h: VTCM ratio PCLKDEN/PCLKNUM 95/31 -> 247/108
    (bridge pixel clock 5.88 -> 7.87 MHz)

INIT_DATA_VERSION is bumped so skip_first_init is not taken: the kernel
re-runs its own SSD2848 init (with the new ratio) instead of trusting
the bootloader's 45Hz programming.

Trade-off: higher display power draw. Revert to go back to 45Hz.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow board/panel specific]

---
--- a/drivers/video/omap2/displays/panel-minnow.c	2026-07-14 22:26:42.432791632 +0200
+++ b/drivers/video/omap2/displays/panel-minnow.c	2026-07-14 22:26:42.445109152 +0200
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@
 		.xres = PANEL_WIDTH,
 		.yres = PANEL_HEIGHT,
 		.pixel_clock = DIV_ROUND_UP(PANEL_WIDTH *
-					    PANEL_HEIGHT * 45, 1000),
+					    PANEL_HEIGHT * 60, 1000),
 		.pixel_format = OMAP_DSS_DSI_FMT_RGB888,
 		.xoffset = 0,
 		.yoffset = 0,
--- a/drivers/video/omap2/displays/panel-minnow-common.h	2026-07-14 22:26:42.433196206 +0200
+++ b/drivers/video/omap2/displays/panel-minnow-common.h	2026-07-14 22:26:42.445179876 +0200
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 
 #ifndef _MINNOW_PANEL_COMMON_HEADER_
 
-#define	INIT_DATA_VERSION	(0x081214) /*MM/DD/YY*/
+#define	INIT_DATA_VERSION	(0x071426) /*MM/DD/YY*/
 /* This header file is used to sync Bootloader and Kernel Display Initialize
  * Structure/Data, please make sure sync it for both Bootloader/Kernel when
  * it changes some settings for Solomon/Orise. Bootloader should pass
@@ -115,13 +115,13 @@
  */
 6, SSD2848_CMD, 0x20, 0x0C, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x02,
 /* VTCM Pixel Clock Frequency Ratio Register[0x0010]
- *   PCLKDEN = 95, PCLKNUM = 31,
- *     Pixel clock = 9.0 x 31 / 95 = 2.94 MHz
+ *   PCLKDEN = 247, PCLKNUM = 108,
+ *     Pixel clock = 9.0 x 108 / 247 = 3.93 MHz
  * since SSD2848 uses 48 bits bus, the actual pixel clock is
  *   depend on current pixel format setting(24 bpp now)
- *   actual pix_clk = 2.94 * 48 / 24 = 5.88 MHz
+ *   actual pix_clk = 3.93 * 48 / 24 = 7.87 MHz
  */
-6, SSD2848_CMD, 0x20, 0x10, 0x00, 0x5F, 0x00, 0x1F,
+6, SSD2848_CMD, 0x20, 0x10, 0x00, 0xF7, 0x00, 0x6C,
 /* VTCM Display Horizontal Configuration Register[0x0014]
  *   Horizontal Total = 392 = 20 + 42 + 320 + 10
  *   Horizontal Display Period Start = 52 (10 + 42)
